    { t: 'Glue & Lake Formation', sub: 'Catalog, ETL and permissions',
      body: `<p><b>AWS Glue</b> crawlers discover schemas and fill the <b>Glue Data Catalog</b> (the shared table definitions Athena, Redshift Spectrum and EMR use). <b>Glue ETL jobs</b> (serverless Spark) clean and convert data; <b>Glue DataBrew</b> does visual prep. <b>Lake Formation</b> adds fine-grained permissions (database, table, column, row) on top of the catalog, in one place instead of many bucket policies.</p>`,
      analogy: `The Glue Data Catalog is the <b>library catalogue</b>: it doesn't hold the books, it says what each book is and where it sits. Lake Formation is the <b>librarian</b> deciding who may read which pages.`,
      hook: `<b>Schema discovery + ETL → Glue. Column/row-level lake permissions → Lake Formation.</b>`,
      words: ['Glue crawler', 'Data Catalog', 'Glue ETL', 'DataBrew', 'Lake Formation', 'column-level security'],
      flow: { from: 'glue', to: 's3', label: 'CRAWL', detail: ['table orders: 14 columns, partition dt', 'Lake Formation: analysts can\'t see card_last4'], color: 'purple' }, focus: ['glue'],
      cmds: [{ c: 'aws glue get-tables --database-name shop --query "TableList[].[Name,StorageDescriptor.SerdeInfo.SerializationLibrary]" --output text', o: 'clicks   org.apache.hadoop.hive.ql.io.parquet.serde.ParquetHiveSerDe\norders   org.apache.hadoop.hive.ql.io.parquet.serde.ParquetHiveSerDe', k: 'cli' }] },
    { t: 'Athena', sub: 'Serverless SQL on S3',
      body: `<p><b>Amazon Athena</b> runs SQL directly on files in S3 using the Glue catalog. No servers, pay per TB scanned, so Parquet and partitions cut the bill. <b>Federated queries</b> reach other sources (DynamoDB, RDS). Typical uses: ad-hoc analysis, querying CloudTrail, VPC Flow Logs and ALB logs.</p>`,
      analogy: `Athena is a <b>search engine for your storage room</b>: ask a question, it reads only the shelves it needs, you pay per shelf read.`,
      hook: `<b>Ad-hoc SQL on S3, serverless, pay per query → Athena.</b>`,
      words: ['Athena', 'serverless SQL', 'per TB scanned', 'federated query', 'CloudTrail logs'],
      flow: { from: 's3', to: 'ath', label: 'SQL', detail: ['SELECT country, sum(total) ... WHERE dt = \'2026-11-13\'', 'scanned 41 MB · $0.0002'], color: 'green' }, focus: ['ath'],
      cmds: [{ c: 'aws athena get-query-execution --query-execution-id $Q --query "QueryExecution.Statistics.[DataScannedInBytes,EngineExecutionTimeInMillis]"', o: '[ 43184110, 1840 ]', k: 'cli' }] },
    { t: 'Redshift', sub: 'The data warehouse',
      body: `<p><b>Amazon Redshift</b> is a columnar, massively parallel <b>data warehouse</b> for complex analytics on terabytes to petabytes, with consistent performance for many BI users. <b>Redshift Serverless</b> removes cluster sizing. <b>Spectrum</b> queries S3 data without loading it. <b>Zero-ETL integrations</b> stream Aurora, RDS and DynamoDB data into Redshift automatically.</p><p>Athena vs Redshift: Athena for occasional queries on the lake; Redshift for heavy, frequent BI with joins across big tables.</p>`,
      analogy: `Athena is <b>renting a car per trip</b>. Redshift is <b>owning a bus</b> for the whole BI team every day.`,
      hook: `<b>OLAP, BI dashboards, complex joins on TB–PB → Redshift.</b> OLTP stays in RDS/Aurora/DynamoDB.`,
      words: ['Redshift', 'data warehouse', 'columnar', 'OLAP', 'Spectrum', 'zero-ETL'],
      flow: { from: 's3', to: 'rs', label: 'LOAD', detail: ['zero-ETL: Aurora orders → Redshift (seconds)'], color: 'amber' }, focus: ['rs'],
      cmds: [{ c: 'aws redshift-serverless list-workgroups --query "workgroups[].[workgroupName,baseCapacity,status]"', o: '[ [ "bi", 32, "AVAILABLE" ] ]', k: 'cli' }] },
    { t: 'EMR, OpenSearch and QuickSight', sub: 'Big data, search, dashboards',
      body: `<p><b>Amazon EMR</b> runs managed <b>Spark, Hadoop, Hive, Presto</b> on EC2, EKS or serverless, for big transformations and ML prep when you need framework control (often with Spot task nodes). <b>OpenSearch Service</b> handles log analytics and full-text search with dashboards. <b>QuickSight</b> is serverless BI: dashboards, ML insights and natural-language questions, connected to Athena, Redshift and more.</p>`,
      analogy: `EMR is a <b>factory floor</b> you configure yourself; QuickSight is the <b>shop window</b> where everyone sees the results.`,
      hook: `<b>Spark/Hadoop → EMR. Logs + search → OpenSearch. Dashboards → QuickSight.</b>`,
      words: ['EMR', 'Spark', 'Hadoop', 'OpenSearch', 'QuickSight', 'BI'],
      flow: { from: 'rs', to: 'qs', label: 'VISUALIZE', detail: ['dashboard: revenue by country, refreshed hourly'], color: 'teal' }, focus: ['emr', 'qs'],
      cmds: [{ c: '# analytics decision table', o: 'real-time stream, custom code  → Kinesis Data Streams\nload stream into S3, no code   → Data Firehose\ncatalog + ETL                  → Glue\nad-hoc SQL on S3               → Athena\nheavy BI, joins, PB            → Redshift\nSpark/Hadoop control           → EMR\ndashboards                     → QuickSight', k: 'exam' }] }
